# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command channels
usage 1   channels                      list audio channels/voices - index, active, envelope level (0-100), muted, core-specific detail (see `mute` to isolate one)

case the fake target's voices
target fake
covers 1
$ channels
out 200
[0] VOICE0   active=True  level=  0 muted=False 
[1] VOICE1   active=False level= 25 muted=False 
[2] VOICE2   active=True  level= 50 muted=False 
[3] VOICE3   active=False level= 75 muted=False noise
status 0
action none
$ mute 1 on
out 16
Channel 1 muted.
status 0
action none
$ channels
out 200
[0] VOICE0   active=True  level=  0 muted=False 
[1] VOICE1   active=False level= 25 muted=True  
[2] VOICE2   active=True  level= 50 muted=False 
[3] VOICE3   active=False level= 75 muted=False noise
status 0
action none
end

case a bare target
target bare
covers 1
$ channels
out 37
(this core reports no audio channels)
status 0
action none
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ channels
out 65
Error: No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
end

